ith 4 mL of cold quenching buffer 1x 3 times. After the last centrifugation, cells are resuspended in 400 μL of Quenching lysis buffer (50mM Tris, 150 mM NaCl, 0.1% SDS, 0.5% sodium deoxycholate, 1% NP-40, 10mM sodium azide, 10 mM sodium ascorbate, 5mM trolox, protease inhibitor (cOmplete EDTA-free, ref 11873580001, Roche) and phosphatase inhibitor (Halt Phosphatase Inhibitor, ref. 78426, Thermo-Fisher Scientific)). After clearing the lysate by centrifuging at 20.000g at 4°C, we loaded the supernatant in a pre-washed Zeba Spin Desalting Column (7K MWCO, ref. 89890, Thermo-Fisher Scientific) and followed the manufacturer’s protocol to remove unreacted biotin-phenol. 10% of the lysates were kept as input and the biotinylated proteins present in the rest of the lysate were purified. 30 μL of pre-washed protease-resistant streptavidin Dynabeads M-280 were added to the samples and incubated at 4°C for 2.5 hours with gentle rotation. The beads were then washed sequentially: 2 times with quenching lysis buffer, 3 times with ammonium bicarbonate 200mM (Sigma, ref. A6141) + 6M Urea (Euromedex, ref. EU0014.A) and 5 times with ammonium bicarbonate 25 mM. Half of the beads were resuspended in 100 μL of ammonium bicarbonate 25 mM and delivered to the proteomic platform, and the other half was resuspended in 20 μL of laemmli buffer (Bio-Rad, ref. 1610747) + 2mM biotin (Sigma, ref. B4501) + 20 mM DTT (Pierce, ref. A39255) for WB analysis.  After delivery to the proteomic platform, the beads were washed trice with 100 μL of 100 mM NH4HCO3, resuspended in 100 μL of 100 mM NH4HCO3 and digested by adding 0.2\u2009μg of trypsin-LysC (Promega) for 1\u2009h at 37 °C. Samples were then loaded into custom-made C18 StageTips packed by stacking three AttractSPE® disk (#SPE-Disks-Bio-C18-100.47.20 Affinisep) into a 200 µL micropipette tip for desalting. Peptides were eluted using a ratio of 40:60 CH3CN:H2O\u2009+\u20090.1% formic acid and vacuum concentrated to dryness with a SpeedVac device.